# RenderType.CompositeState is public final as a class, but 1.20.1's InnerClasses attribute marks it
# protected static final inside RenderType, and that is the flag javac actually enforces -- so
# HudDraw's RenderType.CompositeState.builder() is a compile error on 1.20.1 and was legal on 1.21.1,
# where the nested class was widened to public.
#
# Fabric's answer to an access transformer is an access widener, and this is the one member the whole
# port needs: the HUD's quad layer builds its own render type, and there is no public route to a
# CompositeState in 1.20.1. Applied at build time by Loom and at run time by the loader, so the jar
# carries it and no runtime patch is needed.
accessible class net/minecraft/client/renderer/RenderType$CompositeState
